# Owner-protected: aipass init update and drone @spawn update never write, back up or retire a match.
# One fnmatch pattern per line, relative to the project root. A slashless name matches at any depth;
# a trailing / claims a folder from the root, so */ reaches every seat. A leading / matches nothing.
# Stamped by @spawn at the first seat's birth. These rows are the owner's from here on: edit freely.

# The project's own startup file, cut to what this project needs.
AGENTS.md
# The project's own map: who lives here, its rooms and house rules.
.aipass/tier1_navmap.md
# Every seat's prompt: pure project knowledge, the file the owner edits most.
aipass_local_prompt.md
# Every seat's working layer: drafts, research, post-mortems.
*/docs.local/
# The product's own ignore file: it never takes the AIPass merge, whose lines can hide product paths.
# Slashless, so every seat's .gitignore is held too.
.gitignore

# The product's own files, named by the seat on its first wake. Uncomment and fix each one that exists.
# Never a folder a seat lives in: that row would stop every update to the seat.
# README.md          slashless, so every seat's README is held too
# LICENSE
# .github/
# src/<product_package>/
